# 0012. Mic and camera kill switches; camera off by unloading its driver

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-18

One key cuts the mic, another the camera. The camera is **hard off**: its kernel driver is
unloaded and blocked from loading, through a small root helper allowed by a narrow polkit rule. This is
the first piece of the repo that installs something as root.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: no quick way to cut the mic or camera. A camera switch must be trustworthy: "off" must
  mean no app can reach it, whatever API it uses.
- **State**: new singleton `quickshell/Privacy.qml` with `micOff`, `camState` (`on | off | none | busy`).
- **Mic** (no root): `micOff = true` mutes every PipeWire audio source node (not sink monitors, not app
  streams) via `Quickshell.Services.Pipewire`; while on, newly appearing sources are muted too. `false`
  unmutes the sources it muted. At start `micOff` is read back (true if every source is muted), since
  WirePlumber remembers mute state; the shell keeps no state of its own.
- **Camera helper**: `bin/archminimal-camera`, installed to `/usr/local/bin/archminimal-camera`
  (root:root, 755). Accepts exactly `on | off | status`; anything else exits non-zero.
  - `off`: writes `/etc/modprobe.d/archminimal-camera.conf` = `install uvcvideo /bin/false` (blocks
    loading, also for hot-plugged USB cameras; survives reboot), then `modprobe -r uvcvideo`. If the
    driver is in use it removes the file again, prints `busy`, exits non-zero.
  - `on`: removes the file, `modprobe uvcvideo`.
  - `status`: `off` (file present), `on` (driver loaded), `none` (no file, not loaded, no `/dev/video*`).
- **Polkit**: `/etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-archminimal-camera.rules`: subject in group `wheel` and
  `action.id == "org.freedesktop.policykit.exec"` with `program == "/usr/local/bin/archminimal-camera"`
  → `YES` (no password). Nothing else is allowed.
- **Install**: new `make privacy` target (sudo, asks first; in `make help` and README). `make install`
  stays rootless ([0008](0008-install-by-symlinks-with-backup-ledger.adr)). `make check` reports whether
  helper and rule are installed. Not linked: copied, so a user-writable checkout can't change what root runs.
- **Shell**: `Privacy.qml` runs `status` once at start and after each toggle, no polling
  ([0004](0004-light-by-design.adr)). Toggle: `Quickshell.execDetached`/`Process` with
  `["pkexec", "/usr/local/bin/archminimal-camera", "off"]`; on failure a notification says why
  (e.g. "camera in use"). Helper missing → camera part hidden.
- **No bar module** (changed 2026-11-18, before the first merge): the switches live on keys only. Each switch
  sends a full notification in plain words ("Microphone off", "Camera off", "No camera", …), kept in the
  notification center ([0011](0011-notification-center.adr)) like any other.
- **Keys / IPC**: `Super+Shift+M` mic, `Super+Shift+C` camera (no clashes;
  [0009](0009-keys-described-and-listed-live.adr)); IPC `privacy mic | cam | status`.
- **Consequences**: + camera off holds against every app and across reboots; mic switch is instant.
  − needs a one-time `sudo make privacy`; a root-run helper becomes part of the attack surface (kept to
  three fixed verbs, no arguments passed through); only `uvcvideo` cameras are covered (not e.g. Intel
  IPU6 MIPI cameras); turning the camera off fails while an app uses it.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: PipeWire / WirePlumber, Quickshell `Services.Pipewire`, kmod (`modprobe`), polkit + `pkexec`,
  `hyprpolkitagent` (already installed).
- Alternatives: block the camera in WirePlumber only: no root, but apps opening `/dev/video*` directly
  still reach it; `chmod` on `/dev/video*` via udev: needs root as well and is reset on replug;
  sudoers `NOPASSWD` line: works, but polkit is already the desktop's privilege path; mic via
  `wpctl` commands: extra processes where the Quickshell API does it in place.
